1
00:00:00,017 --> 00:00:02,709
In this town, I paid a dolphin to find my dad.

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:05,404
The storm was over. Dad still hadn't come home.

3
00:00:05,630 --> 00:00:07,225
Only half of his oar had washed up.

4
00:00:07,426 --> 00:00:09,603
I knew that crooked stripe. I'd painted it.

5
00:00:09,904 --> 00:00:11,432
Dad used to feed this dolphin his lunch.

6
00:00:11,692 --> 00:00:13,204
I hoped it knew which way he'd gone.

7
00:00:13,285 --> 00:00:15,189
The search boats all headed out to sea.

8
00:00:15,423 --> 00:00:17,818
The dolphin turned the other way. Toward the reef.

9
00:00:18,044 --> 00:00:19,515
I tied my boat to an old wreck.

10
00:00:19,724 --> 00:00:21,800
The dolphin went under. I went after it.

11
00:00:21,868 --> 00:00:23,262
I thought it had spotted Dad.

12
00:00:23,513 --> 00:00:24,717
It had spotted a chest.

13
00:00:25,017 --> 00:00:27,443
The lid was cracked. I could see gold inside.

14
00:00:27,785 --> 00:00:29,412
I'd have stopped for that any other day.

15
00:00:29,584 --> 00:00:31,988
Then something red slid through a gap in the deck.

16
00:00:32,122 --> 00:00:33,869
The white stripe bent the same way as mine.

17
00:00:34,053 --> 00:00:36,133
The oar moved again. Someone was holding it.

18
00:00:36,276 --> 00:00:37,864
Then I heard him. “Is that you?”

19
00:00:38,074 --> 00:00:39,967
I stuck my hand through the gap. He grabbed it.

20
00:00:40,035 --> 00:00:41,687
Dad told me his boat had hit the reef.

21
00:00:41,847 --> 00:00:43,690
He'd climbed into the part of the wreck above water.

22
00:00:43,866 --> 00:00:45,569
But a beam had fallen across the hatch.

23
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:47,788
I pulled till my feet slipped. Nothing.

24
00:00:47,956 --> 00:00:50,124
Dad pushed from below. It didn't move.

25
00:00:50,458 --> 00:00:52,360
Then I saw the half I'd left in my boat.

26
00:00:52,635 --> 00:00:54,371
I slid the oar under the end of the beam.

27
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:57,521
“Now, Dad!” I leaned down as he pushed up.

28
00:00:57,739 --> 00:01:00,106
The beam rolled clear. The hatch came up.

29
00:01:00,338 --> 00:01:02,615
He reached out. This time I could grab his arm.

30
00:01:02,982 --> 00:01:04,385
I held on till he was in the boat.

31
00:01:04,728 --> 00:01:06,040
We left the gold where it was.

32
00:01:06,607 --> 00:01:08,376
Dad opened our fish box back at the dock.

33
00:01:08,752 --> 00:01:10,089
He held a fish out over the water.

34
00:01:10,298 --> 00:01:11,827
Then he reached in and took out another.

35
00:01:12,169 --> 00:01:13,149
Dad paid him double.

36
00:01:13,325 --> 00:01:14,546
Subscribe if you'd hire him.
